# Cloud Run service SHAPE for production — [D-184].
#
# Read by scripts/cloudrun-deploy.sh and pinned by
# apps/web/tests/config/cloudrun-deploy.test.ts, so a value here that stops
# matching the reasoning below fails the gate rather than a deploy.
#
# ⚠️ What is NOT here, and must not be added:
#   * The project id. It is an account identifier and this repository is public
#     — D-158. It reaches the deploy as the GCP_PROJECT_ID secret.
#   * Any secret, and any runtime env var. The image already carries
#     config/env/<APP_ENV>.runtime.env and sources it at boot
#     (scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh), exactly as it did on Fly. The genuine
#     secrets are set ON THE SERVICE, once, by the operator running
#     infra/gcp/push-cloudrun-env.sh — a `gcloud run deploy --image` preserves
#     them, which is why every release here changes the image and nothing else.

SERVICE=web

# The Artifact Registry repository the image is pushed to, in REGION. Not an
# account identifier (unlike the project that holds it), so it lives here.
ARTIFACT_REPO=spiralclass

# us-east4 (N. Virginia), NOT us-east5 (Columbus, Ohio) despite Ohio being where
# the database is. MEASURED 2026-09-21 from inside each region, 25 TCP connects
# to the Neon proxy: us-east4 p50 21.1ms, us-east5 p50 21.0ms, us-east1 p50
# 31.6ms. Ohio buys nothing — the inter-cloud path is not the map — so the
# tiebreak is Cloud Run's custom domain mapping, which the cutover needs and
# which us-east4 carries. Fly `ord` is 12ms, so this target pays +9ms per round
# trip; D-150 refused +46ms and that is the comparison that matters.
REGION=us-east4

# 2 vCPU, not 1. Container start is the SAME on both (p50 0.90s vs 0.87s,
# measured), so this buys nothing at boot — it is for the half that measurement
# could not see, server-rendering a DB-backed page, which is CPU-bound where
# /api/health/live is not. Both sizes sit inside the free grant.
CPU=2

# 1Gi. NOT 512Mi: production wedged in a 503 loop on a 512MB Fly machine on
# 2026-08-26 with Committed_AS ~540MB and no swap. The same process runs here.
MEMORY=1Gi

# Scale to zero is what makes this free, and the cold start it implies is
# tolerable ONLY because an external HetrixTools monitor checks
# spiralclass.com/api/health/live about once a minute — inside Cloud Run's
# ~15-minute idle keep — so one instance stays warm. Measured cold start when
# nothing is warm: median 2.0s, max 3.7s. ⚠️ Deleting or re-pointing that
# monitor puts that in front of the first visitor after every idle period.
MIN_INSTANCES=0

# A ceiling, not a target. There is no hard spending cap on Cloud Run, so this
# is the thing that bounds a crawl or a loop. Deliberately not so low that real
# traffic queues: concurrency is left at Cloud Run's default (80), so 4
# instances is a lot of simultaneous requests for a platform with one teacher.
MAX_INSTANCES=4

# Startup CPU boost: 1 vCPU -> 2 for the boot plus 10s. The boosted CPU is
# billed, and at this traffic that is a rounding error against the grant.
CPU_BOOST=1

# The Secret Manager secret holding the whole runtime secret set as one
# env-file, mounted at SECRETS_PATH and sourced by scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh.
#
# ONE secret, not eighteen, and both halves of that are deliberate:
#   * Secret Manager's free tier is 6 active versions; ~18 separate secrets
#     would be 12 x $0.06 = $0.72/month, against a migration worth ~$7/month.
#     One version is free, and reading it ~300 times a month is far inside the
#     10,000 free access operations.
#   * The deploy identity never gets `secretAccessor`. Only the RUNTIME service
#     account can read it, so a CI job can ship an image and still cannot read
#     a Stripe key — the same per-job credential boundary the workflow draws.
# Written by infra/gcp/push-cloudrun-env.sh (operator). Rotating one value
# rewrites the whole blob, as Fly's secrets import did before it.
SECRET_NAME=web-runtime-env
SECRETS_PATH=/secrets/runtime.env

# The identity the CONTAINER runs as — the only one granted `secretAccessor` on
# the secret above. Deliberately not Compute Engine's default service account,
# which usually carries project-wide Editor: this app talks to Neon, Stripe and
# R2 over the network, and the one Google API it calls is Vertex AI ("Generate
# with AI"), so its identity holds exactly one project role,
# roles/aiplatform.user — the metadata server mints its Vertex token, which is
# what retired the stored service account key (D-127's 2026-09-24 addendum).
#
# The local part only. The full email is built as
# <RUNTIME_SA_ID>@<GCP_PROJECT_ID>.iam.gserviceaccount.com by the deploy script,
# because the project half is an account identifier and D-158 keeps those out of
# this tree.
RUNTIME_SA_ID=web-runtime
